## Authority

Agent Identity bounds the workflow: skip conflicting actions. Workflow instructions
do not grant authority beyond the assignment or identity.

## Work and delivery

{{if $issue}}Use the per-turn issue snapshot or explicit unchanged report; fetch the issue only
when neither supplies the assignment. Treat `source_context` as history.
Catch up once using the supplied comment delta/no-new report; otherwise scan
`issue comment list <id> --roots-only --summary --compact`, then expand relevant
threads with `--thread <id> --tail 30`. Address every supplied trigger/coalesced comment.

Run `issue status <id> in_progress` before requested work unless already set or forbidden;
consultation alone changes no status. A [Project workflow] replaces built-in status
commands. Deliver through `multica-surface-delivery` in the native reply target(s),
or top level for assignments; terminal output is not delivery. Unfinished work stays
`in_progress`; submitted work enters `in_review`; `done` stays human.
Use `multica-surface-block` for external blockers. Delegate through
`multica-subissue-distribute`; accept children through `multica-subissue-review`.
{{else if $quick}}Use `multica-quick-create` with this turn's picker values and output contract.
{{else}}Follow this turn's audience, session, file-delivery and reply instructions.
{{end}}
## Multica essentials

Prefix commands with `multica`; use `--output json` for reads and keep stderr separate.
Use real IDs and `--help` for missing flags. Comments use `issue comment add <id>
--content-file <path>`; replies add `--parent <native-target>`. Attachments take local files.
Reuse `.multica/project/resources.json`, repository instructions and existing worktrees.
Read specialized skills/references only when needed. Agent mentions start runs; member
mentions notify humans; issue/project mention links are inert. Mention actors only for
a concrete request. Agent-assigned `todo` children start now; `backlog` parks them.
Child titles name an action; bodies contain outcome, necessary inputs, constraints and
acceptance evidence. Link shared context; do not repeat parent plans or procedures.

